\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {26}{\ignorespaces Slices of the reconstructions of $S_0$ through $P$ for $\varepsilon =0.01$, $N=128$ (planes $x=0$, $x=0$, $y=0$, $z=0$; window $[-0.15,0.15]^2$). Light blue: the exact $S_{-\varepsilon }$ and $S_{+\varepsilon }$; grey: the exact $S_0$; red: the reconstruction. Row 1: the vertex interpolations keep the topology of their source (one sheet with a waist, two separate sheets) and miss the pinch at $P$; the SDF interpolation is the cone. Row 2: the deformation is a shift by $\pm k/2$, which cancels: all reconstructions are the cone. Row 3: the spike is in both $S_{\pm \varepsilon }$ and stays. Row 4: different shapes on the two sides; no reconstruction is correct near $P$.}}{62}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:interp-slices}{{26}{62}{}{figure.26}{}}
